  "body": "Same class as #3040. `fold_warnings_located` (`crates/ui/src/operations.rs`) groups warnings by a numeric key, and a group prints only the line of its first warning. `Warning::AvoidHit { part, .. }` uses `216 + part`, so the range is 216..=220. `Warning::UndercutLift` (Slot Undercut, commit 5452810e5, 2026-11-19) uses **217**, the key of an `AvoidHit` on part 1. When the undercut lift comes first, the blocking \"Do not touch\" hit on part 1 folds into the advisory as \"repeated on N more moves\" and is not shown.\n\n#3040 / PR #3062 moves `DrillUndersize` from 216 to 223 and expected `UndercutLift` at 222 (PR #2836's plan). Keys in use on main: 221 is `FirstTraverseLow` and 224 is `FirstTraverseUnderTable`, so 222 is free.\n\nDone means: `UndercutLift` folds under a key outside 216..=220 that no other warning uses (222), and a pinning test folds one `UndercutLift` and one `AvoidHit` on part 1 and asserts both lines are shown, like `a_drill_undersize_never_hides_an_avoid_hit` in #3062.\n",
